{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":445,"recorded_at":1780531400000885,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b292-6916-7d31-aad4-c849da599715"},"task_id":"01a0b292-6916-7d31-aad4-c849da599715","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b292-6916-7d31-aad4-c849da599715","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev2-results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-kkh1an — producer results\n2|\n3|Task: implement the Terminal Instance lifecycle state machine (second\n4|leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe, EPIC M1). Trunk: `c3aae73`\n5|(`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; §§4.B, 4.C, 4.D, 5.2, 7.A\n6|byte-identical to v0.6.0, §13.1 carries the v0.7.0 launch-plan\n7|pure-addition insertion preceding step 2 with the durable\n8|terminal-entry rule text unchanged). The candidate was refreshed onto\n9|`c3aae73` first (`refresh_advanced` with a checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK\n10|replay: trunk's 4qojoz entry kept newest-first, the four 1geqhj\n11|blocks carried verbatim below it): 29 stale trunk-changed paths\n12|restored to the new HEAD, LOGBOOK/README/`decide.go` rebased purely\n13|additive, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical to the new base.\n14|Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot.\n15|\n16|## What was built\n17|\n18|`internal/terminstance` (new package) executes the §4.C lifecycle\n19|contract over the landed `internal/terminalbackend` core, per the\n20|producer scope items (1)-(5):\n21|\n22|- (1) `AXAuthorization` as a closed 7-member object\n23|  (`ParseAXAuthorization`), parsed through the landed `environ`\n24|  closed-shape discipline with the epoch bound witnessed at 1,\n25|  9007199254740991 and both adjacent out-of-range values; every\n26|  engine operation's authorization requirement is a checked object\n27|  (`CheckAuthorization`: kind, expiry, lease identity, lease epoch).\n28|- (2) The closed `RetryDisposition` enum (4 members) carried by every\n29|  result, plus the request/result identity contract\n30|  (`MutationContext`/`MutationResult`, `CheckResult` repetition arms,\n31|  per-row idempotency material through landed `IdempotencyKey`).\n32|- (3) The state-entry rules in `Engine`: receipt before first effect,\n33|  source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` on\n34|  unprovable post-commit errors (never `absent`), `creating` only via\n35|  `create`, `quiescing` only via `quiesce-input`, `stale_fenced` only\n36|  via `ObserveFencing` (landed `fencing` park vocabulary, restore\n37|  operation: launch-class is load-bearing, measured by\n38|  `N-fencing-operation`), per-effect auth+generation rechecks,\n39|  deadline cancels waiting never committed effects.\n40|- (4) The canonical `backend_generation` string[1..256] bound in\n41|  every owned surface (0/257 refuse, 256 admits, characters not\n42|  bytes), with staleness refusing the landed\n43|  `terminal_backend_stale_generation` class; bound verdicts agree\n44|  with landed `GenerationDigest` on the boundary corpus.\n45|- (5) The status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary and request-stop\n46|  rows (sources, targets, effects, key material, evidence\n47|  capabilities, exact refusal sets with outside-set rejection via\n48|  landed `CheckErrorAllowed`), plus the create receipt rule.\n49|\n50|Which existing type or gate each addition extends is tabulated in\n51|`internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md` (Landed extensions); no\n52|second state machine, enum, fencing model, or JSON discipline was\n53|forked.\n54|\n55|This run inherited the rev1 worktree delta verbatim (rev1 never\n56|reached a reviewer: its suite stopped at command 4/30 on the trunk\n57|resumesmoke time bomb, since fixed as `a12d1bd`) and re-verified it\n58|against the spec plus the landed owners. Fixes closed this run: the\n59|staging sweep is age-gated (an ungated sweep deletes a concurrent\n60|`Bind`'s live stage — new keep/sweep tests plus `N-store-sweep-age`);\n61|the `doc.go` drift claim reworded (§13.1 insertion, measured);\n62|missing create entry-deadline and first-effect reported-`stop_timeout`\n63|pins added (the two stop directions now measured together);\n64|previously unmeasured gates rowed (kind mapping, fencing operation,\n65|both timeout-code arms, status source, six `checkParams` arms, the\n66|version-tuple delegation, body scope/member-set, both wire-order\n67|sorts); the bootstrap row caught a weak `err==nil` assertion, now a\n68|literal code+detail refusal. New bounds are stated in TRACEABILITY\n69|(AX-side seam emissions vs row sets, lesser-of-timeout ownership,\n70|document/Go twin masking, engine-scope fail-fast ordering).\n71|\n72|## AC coverage: 72 of 72 rows driven\n73|\n74|Measured, not restated: 72 data rows counted in\n75|`internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`, 70 named top-level tests all\n76|present via `go test -list` and 7 cited subtests all `--- PASS`\n77|(zero missing; see `ratio-check.log`), and the full package suite\n78|green (`terminstance-test-v.log`: exit 0, 168 `--- PASS` including\n79|subtests, 0 `--- FAIL`). Production call sites are named per row in\n80|the matrix.\n81|\n82|## Negative and mutant evidence\n83|\n84|- `mutant_harness.py`: 70/70 rows match on two full passes with\n85|  identical verdict lists — 68 narrowing KILLED + 1 tightening edge\n86|  KILLED + the SURVIVED control. The tightening row\n87|  (`N-auth-epoch-high`) is documented: weakening past `MaxLeaseEpoch`\n88|  is equivalent because `environ` refuses 2^53 at the number layer,\n89|  so the row proves the edge is exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing\n90|  it. Per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in `mutants/pass1/`\n91|  and `mutants/pass2/` (70 plants each, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`,\n92|  no `__pycache__`); production blobs verified byte-identical\n93|  before/after/across passes (`blob-oids-*.txt`).\n94|- Crash/idempotency: no-replace link commits on receipt and\n95|  completion paths, `AfterCommit` hook seam, real-SIGKILL test\n96|  (`TestExecuteCrashChildSelfTerminates`); pending-without-done\n97|  refuses uncertain and recovers through status, never absent.\n98|- No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects\n99|  source text.\n100|\n101|## Predecessor P3 advisories\n102|\n103|- P3-6 closed: `Decision.Descriptor` doc in `internal/axpane/decide.go`\n104|  now states the recorded Binding instance is authoritative on\n105|  reattach (comment-only; axpane suite re-run green: 80.9% cover).\n106|- P3-2/P3-3 stated as unreachable-shape bounds in this leaf's\n107|  TRACEABILITY (no `Decide` caller, no checkpoint loader here).\n108|- P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 left to TASK-260830-2056mm with recovery/events\n109|  reasons (see TRACEABILITY).\n110|\n111|## Validation suite (configured commands, in order)\n112|\n113|Every command below is quoted from `task-board.config.json`\n114|`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` (30 commands) and was\n115|executed once against the exact candidate tree; logs in `cmd/`.\n116|Command 5 ran as 7 bounded chunks with identical flags (sessquery in\n117|3 `-run` shards; every other package whole; each package exactly\n118|once, no flags shortened) because a single shell call is\n119|time-bounded; see `cmd05-summary.txt` and `cmd05-r1..r7.log`.\n120|\n121|| # | Command | Exit |\n122|| --- | --- | --- |\n123|| 1 | `test -z \"$(gofmt -l $(git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard -- '*.go'))\"` | 0 |\n124|| 2 | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n125|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n126|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | 0 (40/40 packages ok) |\n127|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` | 0 (7 chunks, 40/40, 0 DATA RACE) |\n128|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | 0 (40/40; terminstance 83.8%) |\n129|| 7–10 | rpcwire fuzz ×4 (`-fuzztime=100x`) | 0 ×4 |\n130|| 11 | scalar fuzz ×1 | 0 |\n131|| 12–15 | canonicaljson fuzz ×4 | 0 ×4 |\n132|| 16–23 | secconftest fuzz ×8 | 0 ×8 |\n133|| 24 | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (contracts=64, cases=140, clauses 56/569 — trunk figures unchanged) |\n134|| 25 | `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | 0, tree unmodified |\n135|| 26 | `GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n136|| 27 | `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | 0 |\n137|| 28 | `git ls-files -z '*.json' \\| xargs -0 -n1 python3 -c 'import json,sys;json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))'` | 0 |\n138|| 29 | `task-board validate` | 0 (184 pre-existing MISSING_ACTIVITY issues on unrelated elements; zero name this task or story) |\n139|| 30 | `git diff --check` | 0 |\n140|\n141|Full logs in `cmd/` inside\n142|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`. The `.go` tree was\n143|verified byte-identical before and after the race gate\n144|(`go-sha-before-race.txt` == `go-sha-after-race.txt`), so the race\n145|ran against the exact candidate.\n146|\n147|## Files changed\n148|\n149|- `internal/terminstance/` (new package, untracked):\n150|  `doc.go`, `errors.go`, `auth.go`, `disposition.go`, `proof.go`,\n151|  `context.go`, `status.go`, `bodies.go`, `result.go`, `store.go`,\n152|  `fencing.go`, `execute.go`, `mutant_harness.py`,\n153|  `TRACEABILITY.md`, plus 15 test files.\n154|- `internal/axpane/decide.go`: P3-6 doc sentence (comment-only).\n155|- `README.md`: package section (additive).\n156|- `LOGBOOK.md`: leaf entry (additive, newest-first).\n157|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract.\n158|\n159|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n160|\n161|No `ax` command, doctor result, or runtime capability is added.\n162|Binding-object parsing, CLI Result 4, attach/restore/terminate-stale\n163|operations, full create body, credential conditionals, lesser-of\n164|timeout enforcement, and terminal events are stated bounds (see\n165|TRACEABILITY.md). The per-code disposition mapping and the AX-side\n166|seam emission codes are the leaf's contract where the spec pins the\n167|vocabulary but not the mapping.\n168|\n169|## Handoff\n170|\n171|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree;\n172|checklist updated on the board; outcome resources attached:\n173|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md`,\n174|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_conformance-matrix.md`,\n175|`TASK-260830-kkh1an_producer-evidence.tar.gz`.","final_result":true}}}
