{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7a3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":556,"recorded_at":1780531400001107,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b292-9cd5-7431-85d4-a6cb0d1a7a8a"},"task_id":"01a0b292-9cd5-7431-85d4-a6cb0d1a7a8a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b292-9cd5-7431-85d4-a6cb0d1a7a8a","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/fencing.go`.\n1|package terminstance\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n5|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n6|)\n7|\n8|// ObserveFencing projects one AX fencing observation onto the Terminal\n9|// Instance lifecycle. It is the ONLY entry that produces stale_fenced:\n10|// no backend operation targets that state (the landed CheckTransition\n11|// proves it and the engine below never synthesizes it), only AX fencing\n12|// observation does.\n13|//\n14|// The verdict is read entirely from the landed fencing projection: the\n15|// presented local token is authorized against the observation through\n16|// fencing.Authorize with the restore operation, and a ParkStaleOwner\n17|// park — the older-epoch arm and the same-epoch lease-mismatch arm\n18|// alike — moves the local observation to stale_fenced. The operation\n19|// must be launch-class (restore or activation): the input, mutation\n20|// and checkpoint entries refuse a stale token instead of parking it,\n21|// which would surface as an error and never fence. Restore is chosen\n22|// over activation because it gates terminal restore, this story's\n23|// domain; the two are equivalent on the stale arms. Every other\n24|// outcome leaves the state untouched: an\n25|// authorized token reports no transition, and any non-stale refusal or\n26|// park (remote owner, unverified, ambiguous, no winner) surfaces its own\n27|// error with no transition, because only proven staleness fences. A nil\n28|// error with transitioned false is the authorized case.\n29|//\n30|// This function performs no lease comparison of its own: the tuple,\n31|// grant, expiry and direction arms all run inside the landed Authorize,\n32|// so no second fencing model exists here. It reads Winner.LeaseID and\n33|// Winner.Epoch only through Authorize's verdict, never Winner.Checkpoint:\n34|// lease records are immutable content-addressed blobs whose checkpoint\n35|// member is null for every epoch-1 lease, so keying on it would be\n36|// vacuous for every session that never changed hands.\n37|func ObserveFencing(current terminalbackend.InstanceState, presented fencing.PresentedToken, observation fencing.Observation) (terminalbackend.InstanceState, bool, error) {\n38|\tif _, err := terminalbackend.ParseInstanceState(string(current)); err != nil {\n39|\t\treturn current, false, wrapLanded(err)\n40|\t}\n41|\t_, authErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationRestore, presented, observation)\n42|\tif authErr == nil {\n43|\t\treturn current, false, nil\n44|\t}\n45|\tif reason, _, parked := fencing.ParkDetails(authErr); parked && reason == fencing.ParkStaleOwner {\n46|\t\treturn terminalbackend.StateStaleFenced, true, nil\n47|\t}\n48|\treturn current, false, authErr\n49|}","final_result":true}}}
