{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c879","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":663,"recorded_at":1780531400001321,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b292-c99d-7480-b937-6be8a0793426"},"task_id":"01a0b292-c99d-7480-b937-6be8a0793426","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b292-c99d-7480-b937-6be8a0793426","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/terminstance.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n8|\n9|Each row runs M (mutate one production file in place), R (run the\n10|scoped Go killer through the production entry point), V (verdict from\n11|the Go exit code plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test\n12|failure line, SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else —\n13|unapplied patches, build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R\n14|infrastructure errors are ERROR, never kills or survivals. The file is\n15|restored from its backup after every row, pass or fail.\n16|\n17|Row C-control is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that\n18|must SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n19|hard-coding kills.\n20|\n21|Usage:\n22|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/terminstance/mutant_harness.py\n23|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/terminstance/mutant_harness.py N-auth-epoch-low\n24|\"\"\"\n25|\n26|import os\n27|import shutil\n28|import subprocess\n29|import sys\n30|import tempfile\n31|from dataclasses import dataclass\n32|from pathlib import Path\n33|\n34|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n35|PACKAGE = \"internal/terminstance\"\n36|\n37|\n38|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n39|class Mutant:\n40|    name: str\n41|    path: str\n42|    find: str\n43|    replace: str\n44|    count: int\n45|    run: str\n46|    expect: str\n47|    note: str\n48|\n49|\n50|MUTANTS = [\n51|    Mutant(\n52|        name=\"N-auth-epoch-low\",\n53|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/auth.go\",\n54|        find='\\tleaseEpoch, ok := environ.CheckUint53Bounds(members[\"lease_epoch\"], 1, MaxLeaseEpoch)\\n',\n55|        replace='\\tleaseEpoch, ok := environ.CheckUint53Bounds(members[\"lease_epoch\"], 0, MaxLeaseEpoch)\\n',\n56|        count=1,\n57|        run=\"TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound\",\n58|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n59|        note=\"Admits exactly epoch 0; every other out-of-range epoch still refuses.\",\n60|    ),\n61|    Mutant(\n62|        name=\"N-auth-epoch-high\",\n63|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/auth.go\",\n64|        find='\\tleaseEpoch, ok := environ.CheckUint53Bounds(members[\"lease_epoch\"], 1, MaxLeaseEpoch)\\n',\n65|        replace='\\tleaseEpoch, ok := environ.CheckUint53Bounds(members[\"lease_epoch\"], 1, MaxLeaseEpoch-1)\\n',\n66|        count=1,\n67|        run=\"TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound\",\n68|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n69|        note=\"TIGHTENING (the weakening direction is equivalent: environ refuses 2^53 at the number layer, so no weakening past MaxLeaseEpoch is observable; this row proves the edge is exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it).\",\n70|    ),\n71|    Mutant(\n72|        name=\"N-auth-kind\",\n73|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/auth.go\",\n74|        find='\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn \"\", refuse(CodeProtocolError, \"ax authorization kind\")\\n\\t}\\n',\n75|        replace='\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\tif value == \"admin\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn AuthorizationControl, nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn \"\", refuse(CodeProtocolError, \"ax authorization kind\")\\n\\t}\\n',\n76|        count=1,\n77|        run=\"TestParseAXAuthorizationKindClosed\",\n78|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n79|        note=\"Admits exactly the admin kind; every other non-kind still refuses.\",\n80|    ),\n81|    Mutant(\n82|        name=\"N-auth-kind-binding\",\n83|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/auth.go\",\n84|        find=\"\\tif auth.Kind != wantKind {\\n\",\n85|        replace=\"\\tif auth.Kind != wantKind && wantKind != AuthorizationCreate {\\n\",\n86|        count=1,\n87|        run=\"TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/kind_mismatch\",\n88|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n89|        note=\"Admits exactly control authorizations presented as create; other mismatches still refuse.\",\n90|    ),\n91|    Mutant(\n92|        name=\"N-auth-expiry\",\n93|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/auth.go\",\n94|        find=\"\\tif !now.Before(expires) {\\n\",\n95|        replace=\"\\tif !now.Before(expires) && !now.Equal(expires) {\\n\",\n96|        count=1,\n97|        run=\"TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/expiry_edge_refuses\",\n98|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n99|        note=\"Admits exactly the expiry instant; past-expiry instants still refuse.\",\n100|    ),\n101|    Mutant(\n102|        name=\"N-auth-lease-id\",\n103|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/auth.go\",\n104|        find=\"\\tif auth.LeaseID != lease.LeaseID {\\n\",\n105|        replace='\\tif auth.LeaseID != lease.LeaseID && lease.LeaseID != \"6ba7b810-9dad-41d1-80b4-00c04fd430c8\" {\\n',\n106|        count=1,\n107|        run=\"TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/lease_identity_drift\",\n108|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n109|        note=\"Admits exactly the drifted test lease; other identity drifts still refuse.\",\n110|    ),\n111|    Mutant(\n112|        name=\"N-auth-lease-epoch\",\n113|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/auth.go\",\n114|        find=\"\\tif auth.LeaseEpoch != lease.Epoch {\\n\",\n115|        replace=\"\\tif auth.LeaseEpoch != 