\n227|## Stated bounds\n228|\n229|- No `ax` command, no doctor result, no runtime capability claim: the\n230|  `Backend` interface is modeled; tmux/ConPTY/process control and the\n231|  provider process do not exist here.\n232|- Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed-object parsing: no parser\n233|  exists on trunk (`canonicaljson` explicitly rejects\n234|  `urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding`); the generation bound is\n235|  enforced on the surfaces this leaf owns and cited landed for the\n236|  Provider Protocol 3 descriptor (`terminalbackend` checkGeneration\n237|  arms). Full Binding parsing belongs with the provisioning surface.\n238|- CLI Result 4 summary: no landed Result 4 body carries a raw\n239|  generation member (`internal/cliresult` carries none by grep), so\n240|  there is no surface to witness the bound on; consistent with §4.E\n241|  (generation is host-local, non-replicable).\n242|- Attach, restore, terminate-stale, manifest, probe: refused by the\n243|  engine and body scope gates. Restore/terminate-stale recovery and\n244|  terminal binding events belong to the story's final leaf.\n245|- Create is receipt-scoped: receipt, transition, target and headless\n246|  rules execute; the full create body (Binding, Entrypoint,\n247|  presentation transport) belongs to provisioning.\n248|- Credential-realm conditional: credential need is not modeled on the\n249|  engine path.\n250|- Protocol_version membership in the admitted probe list is enforced at\n251|  registry admission (landed), not re-derived per operation; the\n252|  operation gate enforces grammar plus major 1 through the landed\n253|  `CheckVersionTuple` arms.\n254|- The per-code disposition mapping is the leaf's contract where the\n255|  spec pins the vocabulary but not the mapping; every arm is pinned\n256|  literally and mutated.\n257|- AX-side seam emissions are outside the §4.C row sets: the row sets\n258|  govern backend reports (gated through the landed\n259|  `CheckErrorAllowed`), while an uncoded effect outcome classifies\n260|  `terminal_backend_process_failed` and an uncertain retry refuses\n261|  `terminal_backend_unavailable`, both with after `unavailable` and\n262|  `status_first` per the row recovery columns. Engine deadline\n263|  cancels before any attempt report `replay_same` on every row\n264|  (nothing was attempted); a backend-reported `stop_timeout` maps\n265|  through `DispositionFor` (`status_first` even uncommitted) because\n266|  the graceful wait ran. The two stop directions are pinned together\n267|  (`TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes`,\n268|  `TestExecuteBackendRowErrorSets`).\n269|- The wait/stop \"lesser of request deadline and timeout\" bound is\n270|  enforced by the backend wait (modeled here), which reports a coded\n271|  `quiesce_timeout`/`stop_timeout` proving non-commit; the engine\n272|  validates the timeout members (`uint53[1..3600000]`, carried in\n273|  `Params`) and enforces the `MutationContext` deadline.\n274|- Document member arms delegate their grammars to the landed\n275|  `environ`/`scalar` owners and are pinned literally through the\n276|  parse entries; where a Go-level twin re-validates with the same\n277|  detail, the Go twin carries the narrowing row (a document-side\n278|  weakening alone is masked by the twin). The body scope gate and\n279|  the body member-set gate have no twin and carry their own rows\n280|  (`N-body-scope`, `N-body-members`). The engine scope gate is\n281|  fail-fast ordering: admitting an operation past it is masked by\n282|  the `checkParams`/`KeySegments` scope defaults firing the same\n283|  detail (defense in depth, stated); `kindFor` is not redundant and\n284|  carries `N-engine-kind-map`.\n285|- The fencing operation must be launch-class (`restore`, equivalent\n286|  to `activation` on the stale arms and chosen for the terminal\n287|  domain); the non-launch entries refuse stale tokens instead of\n288|  parking them, measured by `N-fencing-operation`.\n289|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract; the final\n290|  leaf carries the registry bindings and the re-pin.\n291|\n292|## Inherited advisories (predecessor P3, for the record)\n293|\n294|- P3-6 closed by this leaf: the `Decision.Descriptor` doc in\n295|  `internal/axpane/decide.go` now states the recorded Binding\n296|  terminal instance ID is authoritative on reattach; this package's\n297|  `doc.go` states the consumer side.\n298|- P3-2 bound stated: this leaf adds no I/O-free `Decide` caller (the\n299|  engine never calls `Decide`), so the missing-closure input shape is\n300|  unreachable from this package; the pure-core hardening stays with\n301|  the owner.\n302|- P3-3 bound stated: this leaf never loads checkpoints (no\n303|  `LoadCheckpoint` caller), so the absent-store shape is unreachable\n304|  from this package.\n305|- P3-1, P3-4, P3-5 left to the final leaf (TASK-260830-2056mm):\n306|  journal-only restore closure (recovery domain), `EmitParked`\n307|  winner binding (events domain) and the corrupt-blob negative\n308|  (recovery domain) belong to events-and-recovery work.","final_result":true}}}
