ackend effect refused\")\\n',\n516|        count=1,\n517|        run=\"TestExecutePostEffectErrorsMoveUnavailable/coded_refusal_on_second_effect\",\n518|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n519|        note=\"Restores source for exactly post-commit process failures; other post-commit errors still fence unavailable.\",\n520|    ),\n521|    Mutant(\n522|        name=\"N-engine-status-match\",\n523|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/execute.go\",\n524|        find=\"\\tif observed.IdentityMatch != computed {\\n\",\n525|        replace=\"\\tif observed.IdentityMatch != computed && observed.State != terminalbackend.StateAbsent {\\n\",\n526|        count=1,\n527|        run=\"TestExecuteStatusMatchedTupleFalseFormRefuses\",\n528|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n529|        note=\"Admits exactly absent-state match lies; other match lies still refuse.\",\n530|    ),\n531|    Mutant(\n532|        name=\"N-engine-status-unknown\",\n533|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/execute.go\",\n534|        find='\\t\\tif code == \"\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn empty, refuse(CodeUnavailable, \"status observation unknown\")\\n\\t\\t}\\n',\n535|        replace='\\t\\tif code == \"\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn StatusReport{State: terminalbackend.StateAbsent}, nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n',\n536|        count=1,\n537|        run=\"TestExecuteStatusUnknownIsNeverAbsent\",\n538|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n539|        note=\"Reports exactly uncoded read failures as absent; coded failures still refuse unknown.\",\n540|    ),\n541|    Mutant(\n542|        name=\"N-engine-status-conditional\",\n543|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/execute.go\",\n544|        find='\\tif body.IncludeProviderObservation && !admitted.Has(\"provider_process_observation\") {\\n',\n545|        replace='\\tif body.IncludeProviderObservation && !admitted.Has(\"provider_process_observation\") && body.TerminalBackendID != \"example.backend\" {\\n',\n546|        count=1,\n547|        run=\"TestExecuteStatusProviderConditional\",\n548|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n549|        note=\"Admits exactly the fixture backend without the provider capability; others still refuse.\",\n550|    ),\n551|    Mutant(\n552|        name=\"N-status-nullpair\",\n553|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/status.go\",\n554|        find=\"\\tif hasInstance != hasGeneration {\\n\",\n555|        replace=\"\\tif hasInstance != hasGeneration && hasInstance {\\n\",\n556|        count=1,\n557|        run=\"TestParseStatusBodyNullPairRule\",\n558|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n559|        note=\"Admits exactly instance-null with generation set; the mirrored half still refuses.\",\n560|    ),\n561|    Mutant(\n562|        name=\"N-interim\",\n563|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/execute.go\",\n564|        find=\"\\tif operation == terminalbackend.OperationCreate {\\n\\t\\treturn terminalbackend.StateCreating\\n\\t}\\n\",\n565|        replace=\"\\tif operation == terminalbackend.OperationCreate || operation == terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput {\\n\\t\\treturn terminalbackend.StateCreating\\n\\t}\\n\",\n566|        count=1,\n567|        run=\"TestExecuteInterimState\",\n568|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n569|        note=\"Enters creating for exactly quiesce-input as well; other operations still observe source.\",\n570|    ),\n571|    Mutant(\n572|        name=\"N-engine-kind-map\",\n573|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/execute.go\",\n574|        find=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput,\\n\\t\\tterminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary,\\n\\t\\tterminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\\n\\t\\treturn AuthorizationControl, true\\n\",\n575|        replace=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput:\\n\\t\\treturn AuthorizationCreate, true\\n\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary,\\n\\t\\tterminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\\n\\t\\treturn AuthorizationControl, true\\n\",\n576|        count=1,\n577|        run=\"TestExecuteQuiesceSuccess\",\n578|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n579|        note=\"Requests exactly create kind for quiesce-input; other operations still map control.\",\n580|    ),\n581|    Mutant(\n582|        name=\"N-fencing-operation\",\n583|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/fencing.go\",\n584|        find=\"\\t_, authErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationRestore, presented, observation)\\n\",\n585|        replace=\"\\t_, authErr := fencing.Authorize(fencing.OperationMutation, presented, observation)\\n\",\n586|        count=1,\n587|        run=\"TestObserveFencingStaleEpochFences\",\n588|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n589|        note=\"Authorizes through exactly the non-launch mutation entry, which refuses stale tokens instead of parking them; the stale observation no longer fences.\",\n590|    ),\n591|    Mutant(\n592|        name=\"N-engine-timeout-code-stop\",\n593|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/execute.go\",\n594|        find=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\\n\\t\\treturn CodeStopTimeout\\n\",\n595|        replace=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\\n\\t\\treturn CodeQuiesceTimeout\\n\",\n596|        count=1,\n597|        run=\"TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes/request-stop\",\n598|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n599|        note=\"Reports exactly the stop deadline as quiesce_timeout; the wait row still reports its own.\",\n600|    ),\n601|    Mutant(\n602|        name=\"N-engine-timeout-code-default\",\n603|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/execute.go\",\n604|        find=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\\n\\t\\treturn CodeStopTimeout\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn CodeTimeout\\n\\t}\\n\",\n605|        replace=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationRequestStop:\\n\\t\\treturn CodeStopTimeout\\n\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn CodeStopTimeout\\n\\t}\\n\",\n606|        count=1,\n607|        run=\"TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes/quiesce-input\",\n608|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n609|        note=\"Reports exactly the default-arm rows (create, quiesce) as stop_timeout; wait and stop still report their own.\",\n610|    ),\n611|    Mutant(\n612|        name=\"N-engine-status-source\",\n613|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/execute.go\",\n614|        find='\\tif source != \"\" {\\n',\n615|        replace='\\tif source != \"\" && source != \"bogus\" {\\n',\n616|        count=1,\n617|        run=\"TestExecuteStatusAllSources\",\n618|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n619|        note=\"Admits exactly the garbage test source past the status matrix; the scripted valid report then succeeds where the killer wants a refusal.\",\n620|    ),\n621|    Mutant(\n622|        name=\"N-params-bootstrap\",\n623|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/context.go\",\n624|        find=\"\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(params.BootstrapOperationID); err != nil {\\n\",\n625|        replace='\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(params.BootstrapOperationID); err != nil && params.BootstrapOperationID != \"nope\" {\\n',\n626|        count=1,\n627|        run=\"TestCheckMutationContextParams\",\n628|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n629|        note=\"Admits exactly the nope bootstrap; other malformed bootstraps still refuse.\",\n630|    ),\n631|    Mutant(\n632|        name=\"N-params-quiescence-quiesce\",\n633|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/context.go\",\n634|        find=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput:\\n\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(params.QuiescenceGeneration); err != nil {\\n\",\n635|        replace='\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationQuiesceInput:\\n\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(params.QuiescenceGeneration); err != nil && params.QuiescenceGeneration != \"nope\" {\\n',\n636|        count=1,\n637|        run=\"TestCheckMutationContextParams\",\n638|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n639|        note=\"Admits exactly the nope quiescence generation on the quiesce arm; the wait arm still refuses it.\",\n640|    ),\n641|    Mutant(\n642|        name=\"N-params-quiescence-wait\",\n643|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/context.go\",\n644|        find=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\\n\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(params.QuiescenceGeneration); err != nil {\\n\",\n645|        replace='\\tcase terminalbackend.OperationWaitSafeBoundary:\\n\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(params.QuiescenceGeneration); err != nil && params.QuiescenceGeneration != \"nope\" {\\n',\n646|        count=1,\n647|        run=\"TestCheckMutationContextParams\",\n648|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n649|        note=\"Admits exactly the nope quiescence generation on the wait arm; the quiesce arm still refuses it.\",\n650|    ),\n651|    Mutant(\n652|        name=\"N-params-proof\",\n653|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/context.go\",\n654|        find=\"\\t\\tif _, err := ParseProviderProofKind(string(params.ProviderProofKind)); err != nil {\\n\",\n655|        replace='\\t\\tif _, err := ParseProviderProofKind(string(params.ProviderProofKind)); err != nil && string(params.ProviderProofKind) != \"provider_restart\" {\\n',\n656|        count=1,\n657|        run=\"TestCheckMutationContextParams\",\n658|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n659|        note=\"Admits exactly the provider_restart proof; other malformed proofs still refuse.\",\n660|    ),\n661|    Mutant(\n662|        name=\"N-params-evidence\",\n663|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/context.go\",\n664|        find=\"\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseDigest(params.SafeBoundaryEvidenceID); err != nil {\\n\",\n665|        replace='\\t\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseDigest(params.SafeBoundaryEvidenceID); err != nil && params.SafeBoundaryEvidenceID != \"not-a-digest\" {\\n',\n666|        count=1,\n667|        run=\"TestCheckMutationContextParams\",\n668|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n669|        note=\"Admits exactly the not-a-digest stop evidence; other malformed evidence still refuses.\",\n670|    ),\n671|    Mutant(\n672|        name=\"N-params-graceful\",\n673|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/context.go\",\n674|        find=\"\\t\\tif params.GracefulTimeoutMs < 1 || params.GracefulTimeoutMs > 3600000 {\\n\",\n675|        replace=\"\\t\\tif params.GracefulTimeoutMs < 1 || params.GracefulTimeoutMs > 3600001 {\\n\",\n676|        count=1,\n677|        run=\"TestCheckMutationContextParams\",\n678|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n679|        note=\"Admits exactly graceful timeout 3600001; other out-of-bound graceful timeouts still refuse.\",\n680|    ),\n681|    Mutant(\n682|        name=\"N-version-delegation\",\n683|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/context.go\",\n684|        find=\"\\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckVersionTuple(backendID, implementationVersion, protocolVersion, []string{protocolVersion}); err != nil {\\n\",\n685|        replace='\\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckVersionTuple(backendID, implementationVersion, protocolVersion, []string{protocolVersion}); err != nil && backendID != \"example.backend\" {\\n',\n686|        count=1,\n687|        run=\"TestParseMutationContextMemberRefusals\",\n688|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n689|        note=\"Skips the landed version-tuple delegation for exactly the fixture backend; other backends still gate.\",\n690|    ),\n691|    Mutant(\n692|        name=\"N-body-scope\",\n693|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/bodies.go\",\n694|        find=\"\\tif _, ok := operationBodyMembers[parsed]; !ok {\\n\",\n695|        replace=\"\\tif _, ok := operationBodyMembers[parsed]; !ok && parsed != terminalbackend.OperationCreate {\\n\",\n696|        count=1,\n697|        run=\"TestParseOperationBodyScopeGate\",\n698|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n699|        note=\"Admits exactly create past the body scope map; the member-count arm then fires with a different detail, failing the scope killer.\",\n700|    ),\n701|    Mutant(\n702|        name=\"N-body-members\",\n703|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/bodies.go\",\n704|        find=\"\\tif len(object) != len(want) {\\n\",\n705|        replace=\"\\tif len(object) != len(want) && len(object) != len(want)+1 {\\n\",\n706|        count=1,\n707|        run=\"TestParseOperationBodyRefusals\",\n708|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n709|        note=\"Admits exactly one-extra-member bodies, silently ignoring the smuggled member; other shapes still refuse.\",\n710|    ),\n711|    Mutant(\n712|        name=\"N-store-sweep-age\",\n713|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/store.go\",\n714|        find=\"\\t\\tif now.Sub(info.ModTime()) < stagingSweepAge {\\n\",\n715|        replace='\\t\\tif now.Sub(info.ModTime()) < stagingSweepAge && !strings.HasSuffix(entry.Name(), \"-live.tmp\") {\\n',\n716|        count=1,\n717|        run=\"TestStoreSweepKeepsLiveStaging\",\n718|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n719|        note=\"Sweeps exactly live-suffixed young staging; other young files are still kept.\",\n720|    ),\n721|    Mutant(\n722|        name=\"N-result-effects-sort\",\n723|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/result.go\",\n724|        find=\"\\tsort.Slice(ordered, func(i, j int) bool { return ordered[i] < ordered[j] })\\n\",\n725|        replace=\"\\tsort.Slice(ordered, func(i, j int) bool { return ordered[i] > ordered[j] })\\n\",\n726|        count=1,\n727|        run=\"TestBuildResultSortsEffectsAndEvidence\",\n728|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n729|        note=\"Reports exactly the inverted effect order; the evidence order still sorts ascending.\",\n730|    ),\n731|    Mutant(\n732|        name=\"N-result-evidence-sort\",\n733|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/result.go\",\n734|        find=\"\\tsort.Strings(orderedEvidence)\\n\",\n735|        replace=\"\\tsort.Sort(sort.Reverse(sort.StringSlice(orderedEvidence)))\\n\",\n736|        count=1,\n737|        run=\"TestBuildResultSortsEffectsAndEvidence\",\n738|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n739|        note=\"Reports exactly the inverted evidence order; the effect order still sorts ascending.\",\n740|    ),\n741|    Mutant(\n742|        name=\"C-control\",\n743|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/doc.go\",\n744|        find=\"// Composition, not re-implementation: the eight-state enum, the ten-operation\\n\",\n745|        replace=\"// Composition, not re-implementation (control): the eight-state enum, the ten-operation\\n\",\n746|        count=1,\n747|        run=\"TestRequiresProviderObservation\",\n748|        expect=\"SURVIVED\",\n749|        note=\"Harmless control: a comment-only edit must survive.\",\n750|    ),\n751|]\n752|\n753|\n754|def run_mutant(mutant: Mutant) -> str:\n755|    target = REPO / mutant.path\n756|    original = target.read_text()\n757|    found = original.count(mutant.find)\n758|    if found != mutant.count:\n759|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: patch anchors {found}, want {mutant.count}\"\n760|    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as staging:\n761|        backup = Path(staging) / \"backup\"\n762|        shutil.copy2(target, backup)\n763|        try:\n764|            target.write_text(original.replace(mutant.find, mutant.replace))\n765|            run = subprocess.run(\n766|                [\"go\", \"test\", f\"./{PACKAGE}/\", \"-run\", mutant.run, \"-count=1\"],\n767|                cwd=REPO,\n768|                capture_output=True,\n769|                text=True,\n770|                timeout=300,\n771|            )\n772|        finally:\n773|            shutil.copy2(backup, target)\n774|    output = (run.stdout + run.stderr).strip()\n775|    if os.environ.get(\"AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE\") == \"1\":\n776|        print(f\"--- raw: {mutant.name}: exit {run.returncode} ---\", flush=True)\n777|        print(output, flush=True)\n778|        print(f\"--- end raw: {mutant.name} ---\", flush=True)\n779|    if 'build failed' in output or '\\n# ' in output or output.startswith('# '):\n780|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: build broke under the patch\"\n781|    if run.returncode == 0:\n782|        verdict = \"SURVIVED\"\n783|    elif '--- FAIL' in output or 'FAIL:' in output:\n784|        verdict = \"KILLED\"\n785|    else:\n786|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: exit {run.returncode} with no kill line\"\n787|    mark = \"ok\" if verdict == mutant.expect else \"MISMATCH\"\n788|    return f\"{mark}: {mutant.name}: {verdict} (want {mutant.expect}) :: {mutant.note} [exit {run.returncode}]\"\n789|\n790|\n791|def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n792|    selected = [m for m in MUTANTS if not argv or m.name in argv]\n793|    if argv and len(selected) != len(argv):\n794|        unknown = sorted(set(argv) - {m.name for m in selected})\n795|        print(f\"unknown mutants: {', '.join(unknown)}\")\n796|        return 2\n797|    failures = 0\n798|    for mutant in selected:\n799|        try:\n800|            line = run_mutant(mutant)\n801|        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n802|            line = f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: killer timed out\"\n803|        print(line, flush=True)\n804|        if not line.startswith(\"ok:\"):\n805|            failures += 1\n806|    return 1 if failures else 0\n807|\n808|\n809|if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n810|    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":696,"recorded_at":1780531400001387,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"call_id":"call_01a0b292d533730fb7a907708a8660ba","text":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# internal/terminstance — TRACEABILITY\n2|\n3|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §4.B (generation bound),\n4|§4.C (lifecycle and operations), §4.D (capability conditionals), §5.2\n5|(status/unknown discipline), §7.A (descriptor generation binding, cited\n6|landed), §13.1 (durable terminal entry before provider launch). Every\n7|row names the production entry and the committed test that drives it;\n8|every expectation asserts the literal specification token at the entry.\n9|Coverage: **72 of 72 AC rows driven** (counted below; verified by\n10|`go test ./internal/terminstance/ -count=1 -v`).\n11|\n12|## Landed extensions\n13|\n14|Every addition extends a landed type or gate; nothing is forked:\n15|\n16|| Addition | Extends |\n17|| --- | --- |\n18|| `ParseAXAuthorization`, `CheckAuthorization` | `terminalbackend.ParseAttachAuthorization` twin (shape discipline, strict expiry, binding checks); frame and member grammars delegated to `environ`/`scalar` |\n19|| `ParseRetryDisposition`, `DispositionFor` | New leaf contract over the landed row-code vocabulary (`terminalbackend` code consts aliased, never retyped) |\n20|| `ParseProviderProofKind`, `RequiresProviderObservation` | New leaf contract over the §4.C proof vocabulary |\n21|| `ParseMutationContext`, `CheckMutationContext`, `KeySegments` | `terminalbackend.IdempotencyKey` shapes, `ParseID`, `CheckVersionTuple`, `GenerationDigest` |\n22|| `ParseOperationBody`, `ParseStatusBody` | `environ.DecodeStrictObject` closed-shape discipline |\n23|| `Result`, `CheckResult` | `terminalbackend` state/effect vocabularies, `scalar` digests |\n24|| `Engine.ExecuteMutating`, `ExecuteStatus` | `terminalbackend.CheckTransition`, `CheckErrorAllowed`, `CheckOperation`, `CheckStatusResult` |\n25|| `ReceiptStore` | `terminalbackend.Receipt`/`Ledger`/`ImportLedger` triple and line encoding (byte-agreed, crash-durable) |\n26|| `ObserveFencing` | `fencing.Authorize` + `ParkDetails` (stale verdict only; no local tuple comparison) |\n27|| Engine error codes | `terminalbackend` code consts aliased; the four literals the landed core spells only inside its allowed-error table (`terminal_backend_timeout`, `terminal_backend_process_failed`, `quiesce_timeout`, `stop_timeout`) pinned admitted by `TestRowCodesAreAdmittedByCheckErrorAllowed` |\n28|\n29|## AC rows\n30|\n31|### AXAuthorization (item 1) — `ParseAXAuthorization`, `CheckAuthorization`\n32|\n33|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n34|| --- | --- | --- |\n35|| 1 | Closed 7-member object admitted, every member literal | `TestParseAXAuthorizationAdmitsClosedFixture` |\n36|| 2 | lease_id is UUIDv4 (v7, garbage, number refuse) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n37|| 3 | lease_epoch 1 admitted | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n38|| 4 | lease_epoch 9007199254740991 admitted | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n39|| 5 | lease_epoch 0 refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n40|| 6 | lease_epoch 9007199254740992 refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochBound` |\n41|| 7 | Epoch AX number model (fraction, exponent, sign, string, bool, null, huge refuse) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationEpochNumberModel` |\n42|| 8 | holder_host_id is UUIDv7 | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n43|| 9 | authorization_kind closed create/control/force_stale/restore | `TestParseAXAuthorizationKindClosed` |\n44|| 10 | Strict expiry (equal and inverted refuse unauthorized) | `TestParseAXAuthorizationStrictExpiry` |\n45|| 11 | authorization_evidence_id is a digest | `TestParseAXAuthorizationMemberTypes` |\n46|| 12 | Unknown member refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n47|| 13 | Missing member refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n48|| 14 | Frame violations (non-object, trailing, duplicate, surrogate, non-UTF8) refused | `TestParseAXAuthorizationClosedShape` |\n49|| 15 | Kind binding (control presented as create refuses) | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/kind_mismatch` |\n50|| 16 | Expiry at and past the edge refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/expired`, `/expiry_edge_refuses` |\n51|| 17 | Lease identity drift refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/lease_identity_drift` |\n52|| 18 | Lease epoch drift refuses | `TestCheckAuthorizationRefusals/lease_epoch_drift` |\n53|\n54|### Closed enums (item 2) — `ParseRetryDisposition`, `ParseProviderProofKind`, `ParseAuthorizationKind`, `DispositionFor`\n55|\n56|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n57|| --- | --- | --- |\n58|| 19 | RetryDisposition closed replay_same/status_first/new_authorization/required_operator_action | `TestParseRetryDispositionClosed`, `TestClosedEnumsAreExactlyPinned` |\n59|| 20 | Per-code disposition mapping (26 literal rows) | `TestDispositionForMapping` |\n60|| 21 | ProviderProofKind closed provider_quiescence/provider_process_exit/ax_checkpoint_boundary | `TestParseProviderProofKindClosed`, `TestClosedEnumsAreExactlyPinned` |\n61|| 22 | Provider classification (2 provider kinds, AX boundary not) | `TestRequiresProviderObservation` |\n62|| 23 | AuthorizationKind closed create/control/force_stale/restore | `TestParseAuthorizationKindClosed`, `TestClosedEnumsAreExactlyPinned` |\n63|\n64|### Request identity (item 2) — `ParseMutationContext`, `CheckMutationContext`, `KeySegments`\n65|\n66|| # | Clause | Committed test |\n67|| --- | --- | --- |\n68|| 24 | Closed 10-member context admitted, every member literal | `TestParseMutati