{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9e3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":844,"recorded_at":1780531400001683,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b294-7098-7f21-b0df-845afed41e40"},"task_id":"01a0b294-7098-7f21-b0df-845afed41e40","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b294-7098-7f21-b0df-845afed41e40","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/spec4c.md`.\n1|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n2|\n3|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n4|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n5|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n6|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n7|\n8|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n9|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n10|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n11|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n12|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n13|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n14|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n15|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n16|\n17|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n18|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n19|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n20|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n21|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n22|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n23|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n24|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n25|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n26|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n27|\n28|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n29|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n30|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n31|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n32|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n33|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n34|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n35|\n36|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n37|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n38|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n39|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n40|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n41|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n42|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n43|\n44|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n45|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n46|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n47|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n48|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n49|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n50|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n51|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n52|\n53|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n54|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n55|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n56|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n57|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n58|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n59|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n60|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n61|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n62|\n63|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n64|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n65|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n66|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n67|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n68|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n69|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n70|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n71|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n72|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n73|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n74|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n75|\n76|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n77|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n78|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n79|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n80|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n81|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n82|persisted or replicated.\n83|\n84|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n85|| --- | --- | --- |\n86|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n87|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n88|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n89|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n90|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n91|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n92|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n93|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n94|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n95|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n96|\n97|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n98|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n99|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n100|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n101|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n102|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n103|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n104|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n105|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n106|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n107|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n108|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n109|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n110|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n111|\n112|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n113|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n114|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n115|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n116|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n117|transition and no side effect.\n118|\n119|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n120|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n121|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n122|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n123|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n124|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n125|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n126|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n127|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n128|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n129|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n130|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n131|\n132|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n133|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n134|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n135|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n136|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n137|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n138|\n139|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n140|\n141|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n142|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n143|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n144|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n145|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n146|\n147|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n148|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n149|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n150|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n151|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n152|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n153|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n154|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n155|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n156|\n157|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n158|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n159|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n160|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n161|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n162|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n163|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n164|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n165|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n166|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n167|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n168|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n169|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n170|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n171|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n172|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n173|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n174|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n175|\n176|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n177|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n178|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n179|member is permitted:\n180|\n181|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n182|| --- | --- |\n183|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n184|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n185|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n186|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n187|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n188|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n189|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n190|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n191|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n192|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n193|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n194|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n195|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n196|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n197|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n198|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n199|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n200|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n201|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n202|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n203|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n204|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n205|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n206|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n207|\n208|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n209|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n210|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n211|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n212|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n213|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n214|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n215|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n216|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n217|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n218|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n219|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n220|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n221|change and before activation.\n222|\n223|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n224|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n225|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n226|activation when policy allows.\n227|\n228|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n229|\n230|| Classification | Members and rule |\n231|| --- | --- |\n232|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n233|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n234|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n235|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n236|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n237|\n238|Presentation transport is exactly <code>local_only</code>,\n239|<code>trusted_private_mesh</code>, or <code>third_party_relay</code>. Current AX\n240|admits only the first two. A relay-required/public-service backend is unavailable\n241|pending explicit future product/contract approval. AX retains no permanent\n242|public TCP listener. Attach transport carries no AX authoritative state,\n243|provider store, workspace, Checkpoint, task-board data, or ownership change.\n244|\n245|The exact v0.4.3 Configuration 1/2 <code>tmux|conpty</code>, Provider Protocol 2\n246|TerminalDescriptor, Session Event 1 terminal payloads, and CLI Result 1 start/\n247|resume shapes and digests remain immutable. Version adapters deterministically\n248|map legacy <code>tmux</code> to <code>ax.tmux</code> and <code>conpty</code> to\n249|<code>ax.conpty</code>, with version/generation <code>legacy_unreported</code>\n250|and no inferred capabilities. Reverse projection exists only for those two IDs;\n251|other IDs return <code>incompatible_schema</code>, never fallback. Translation\n252|never rewrites or re-digests history.\n253|\n254|New readers accept old objects through the adapter. Old readers may browse/sync\n255|opaque newer immutable records but cannot activate, restore, or write them.\n256|Mixed peers negotiate each containing contract independently; no common backend\n257|major means browse/sync only. Unknown/unsupported IDs remain visible as unknown/\n258|unavailable; registry read failure is never absence. Lower-version writers are\n259|read-only and cannot write downgrade replacements. Bootstrap permits only a\n260|framed <code>manifest</code> call in an understood major. Capability negotiation\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9e5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":845,"recorded_at":1780531400001685,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b294-7098-7f21-b0df-845afed41e40"},"task_id":"01a0b294-7098-7f21-b0df-845afed41e40","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b294-7098-7f21-b0df-845afed41e40"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9e7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":846,"recorded_at":1780531400001687,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"call_id":"call_01a0b2946c3d73039944b5ef260cedb9","text":"Read text file `/tmp/spec4c.md`.\n1|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n2|\n3|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n4|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n5|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n6|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n7|\n8|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n9|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n10|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n11|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n12|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n13|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n14|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n15|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n16|\n17|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n18|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n19|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n20|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n21|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n22|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n23|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n24|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n25|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n26|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n27|\n28|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n29|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n30|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n31|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n32|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n33|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n34|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n35|\n36|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n37|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n38|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n39|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n40|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n41|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n42|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n43|\n44|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n45|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n46|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n47|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n48|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n49|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n50|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n51|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n52|\n53|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n54|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n55|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n56|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n57|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n58|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n59|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n60|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n61|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n62|\n63|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n64|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n65|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n66|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n67|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n68|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n69|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n70|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n71|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n72|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n73|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n74|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n75|\n76|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n77|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n78|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n79|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n80|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n81|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n82|persisted or replicated.\n83|\n84|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n85|| --- | --- | --- |\n86|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n87|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n88|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n89|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n90|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n91|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n92|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n93|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n94|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n95|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n96|\n97|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n98|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n99|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n100|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n101|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n102|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n103|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n104|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n105|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n106|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n107|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n108|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n109|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n110|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n111|\n112|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n113|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n114|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n115|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n116|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n117|transition and no side effect.\n118|\n119|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n120|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n121|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n122|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n123|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n124|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n125|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n126|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n127|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n128|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n129|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n130|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n131|\n132|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n133|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n134|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n135|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n136|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n137|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n138|\n139|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n140|\n141|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n142|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n143|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n144|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n145|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n146|\n147|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n148|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n149|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n150|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n151|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n152|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n153|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n154|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n155|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n156|\n157|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n158|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n159|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n160|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n161|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n162|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n163|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n164|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n165|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n166|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n167|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n168|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n169|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n170|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n171|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n172|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n173|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n174|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n175|\n176|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n177|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n178|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n179|member is permitted:\n180|\n181|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n182|| --- | --- |\n183|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n184|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n185|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n186|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n187|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n188|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n189|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n190|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n191|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n192|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n193|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n194|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n195|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n196|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n197|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n198|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n199|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n200|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n201|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n202|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n203|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n204|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n205|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n206|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n207|\n208|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n209|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n210|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n211|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n212|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n213|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n214|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n215|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n216|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n217|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n218|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n219|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n220|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n221|change and before activation.\n222|\n223|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n224|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n225|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n226|activation when policy allows.\n227|\n228|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n229|\n230|| Classification | Members and rule |\n231|| --- | --- |\n232|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n233|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n234|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n235|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n236|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n237|\n238|Presentation transport is exactly <code>local_only</code>,\n239|<code>trusted_private_mesh</code>, or <code>third_party_relay</code>. Current AX\n240|admits only the first two. A relay-required/public-service backend is unavailable\n241|pending explicit future product/contract approval. AX retains no permanent\n242|public TCP listener. Attach transport carries no AX authoritative state,\n243|provider store, workspace, Checkpoint, task-board data, or ownership change.\n244|\n245|The exact v0.4.3 Configuration 1/2 <code>tmux|conpty</code>, Provider Protocol 2\n246|TerminalDescriptor, Session Event 1 terminal payloads, and CLI Result 1 start/\n247|resume shapes and digests remain immutable. Version adapters deterministically\n248|map legacy <code>tmux</code> to <code>ax.tmux</code> and <code>conpty</code> to\n249|<code>ax.conpty</code>, with version/generation <code>legacy_unreported</code>\n250|and no inferred capabilities. Reverse projection exists only for those two IDs;\n251|other IDs return <code>incompatible_schema</code>, never fallback. Translation\n252|never rewrites or re-digests history.\n253|\n254|New readers accept old objects through the adapter. Old readers may browse/sync\n255|opaque newer immutable records but cannot activate, restore, or write them.\n256|Mixed peers negotiate each containing contract independently; no common backend\n257|major means browse/sync only. Unknown/unsupported IDs remain visible as unknown/\n258|unavailable; registry read failure is never absence. Lower-version writers are\n259|read-only and cannot write downgrade replacements. Bootstrap permits only a\n260|framed <code>manifest</code> call in an understood major. Capability negotiation\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
