{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca1d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":873,"recorded_at":1780531400001741,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b297-7904-7bf0-a519-bd44fa0beab2"},"task_id":"01a0b297-7904-7bf0-a519-bd44fa0beab2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b297-7904-7bf0-a519-bd44fa0beab2","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/disposition.go`.\n1|package terminstance\n2|\n3|// RetryDisposition is the closed §4.C retry disposition enum. Every\n4|// result carries exactly one.\n5|type RetryDisposition string\n6|\n7|// Retry dispositions.\n8|const (\n9|\tDispositionReplaySame             RetryDisposition = \"replay_same\"\n10|\tDispositionStatusFirst            RetryDisposition = \"status_first\"\n11|\tDispositionNewAuthorization       RetryDisposition = \"new_authorization\"\n12|\tDispositionRequiredOperatorAction RetryDisposition = \"required_operator_action\"\n13|)\n14|\n15|// ParseRetryDisposition admits exactly the four §4.C dispositions.\n16|func ParseRetryDisposition(value string) (RetryDisposition, error) {\n17|\tswitch RetryDisposition(value) {\n18|\tcase DispositionReplaySame, DispositionStatusFirst,\n19|\t\tDispositionNewAuthorization, DispositionRequiredOperatorAction:\n20|\t\treturn RetryDisposition(value), nil\n21|\tdefault:\n22|\t\treturn \"\", refuse(CodeProtocolError, \"retry disposition vocabulary\")\n23|\t}\n24|}\n25|\n26|// DispositionFor maps a terminal failure code to its retry disposition.\n27|// committed reports whether any side effect committed before the failure:\n28|// an error before the first effect restores the source state and may be\n29|// retried or refused by class, while an error after a committed effect\n30|// whose result cannot be proven funnels to status_first, because only a\n31|// successful status read proves what happened. The spec pins the\n32|// disposition vocabulary but not the per-code mapping, so this mapping is\n33|// the leaf's contract, pinned literally per arm:\n34|//\n35|//   - terminal_backend_unauthorized names its own remedy in both cases:\n36|//     the lease moved or lapsed and status cannot fix auth.\n37|//   - terminal_backend_timeout and quiesce_timeout are clean before any\n38|//     commit (retry the identical wait) and uncertain after one.\n39|//   - stop_timeout, idempotency_mismatch, terminal_backend_stale_generation,\n40|//     local_precondition_failed and terminal_backend_unavailable always\n41|//     route through status: a stop wait, a window conflict, a drifted\n42|//     generation, a refused precondition and an unserved backend all\n43|//     require a fresh observation before any retry.\n44|//   - terminal_backend_capability_unproven,\n45|//     terminal_backend_integrity_failure, terminal_backend_process_failed,\n46|//     terminal_backend_protocol_error and any unknown code stop automation\n47|//     before any commit (an operator must prove the capability, heal the\n48|//     backend, or fix the caller) and route through status after one,\n49|//     because the committed effect's result is then unproven.\n50|//\n51|// A code the row forbids never reaches here: the engine routes backend\n52|// reports through CheckErrorAllowed first, so the default arm below fires\n53|// only for an uncoded failure the engine classified itself.\n54|func DispositionFor(code string, committed bool) RetryDisposition {\n55|\tswitch code {\n56|\tcase CodeUnauthorized:\n57|\t\treturn DispositionNewAuthorization\n58|\tcase CodeTimeout, CodeQuiesceTimeout:\n59|\t\tif committed {\n60|\t\t\treturn DispositionStatusFirst\n61|\t\t}\n62|\t\treturn DispositionReplaySame\n63|\tcase CodeStopTimeout, CodeIdempotencyMismatch, CodeStaleGeneration,\n64|\t\tCodePreconditionFailed, CodeUnavailable:\n65|\t\treturn DispositionStatusFirst\n66|\tdefault:\n67|\t\tif committed {\n68|\t\t\treturn DispositionStatusFirst\n69|\t\t}\n70|\t\treturn DispositionRequiredOperatorAction\n71|\t}\n72|}","final_result":true}}}
