{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cae5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":973,"recorded_at":1780531400001941,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b297-f7ed-77e3-a709-8bfc86be81ce"},"task_id":"01a0b297-f7ed-77e3-a709-8bfc86be81ce","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b297-f7ed-77e3-a709-8bfc86be81ce","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/errors.go`.\n1|package terminstance\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\n6|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n7|)\n8|\n9|// Wire error codes this package may report. Every code shared with the\n10|// landed core is a const alias of the landed constant, so the literal is\n11|// spelled once on trunk: retyping it here would fork the vocabulary. The\n12|// four row codes the landed core spells only as string literals inside\n13|// its allowed-error table are spelled literally here and pinned equal to\n14|// the landed table by TestRowCodesAreAdmittedByCheckErrorAllowed, which\n15|// drives each literal through the landed CheckErrorAllowed for its row.\n16|const (\n17|\tCodeProtocolError       = terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError\n18|\tCodeUnauthorized        = terminalbackend.CodeUnauthorized\n19|\tCodeUnavailable         = terminalbackend.CodeUnavailable\n20|\tCodePreconditionFailed  = terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed\n21|\tCodeIdempotencyMismatch = terminalbackend.CodeIdempotencyMismatch\n22|\tCodeStaleGeneration     = terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration\n23|\tCodeCapabilityUnproven  = terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven\n24|\tCodeIntegrityFailure    = terminalbackend.CodeIntegrityFailure\n25|\t// CodeTimeout is the §4.C terminal_backend_timeout row code.\n26|\tCodeTimeout = \"terminal_backend_timeout\"\n27|\t// CodeProcessFailed is the §4.C terminal_backend_process_failed row code.\n28|\tCodeProcessFailed = \"terminal_backend_process_failed\"\n29|\t// CodeQuiesceTimeout is the §4.C quiesce_timeout row code, admitted\n30|\t// only on wait-safe-boundary.\n31|\tCodeQuiesceTimeout = \"quiesce_timeout\"\n32|\t// CodeStopTimeout is the §4.C stop_timeout row code, admitted only\n33|\t// on request-stop.\n34|\tCodeStopTimeout = \"stop_timeout\"\n35|)\n36|\n37|// Error is a lifecycle refusal. Code is always one of the Code* constants;\n38|// Detail is a static clause: it never echoes identities, generations,\n39|// keys, digests, or other local data.\n40|type Error struct {\n41|\tCode   string\n42|\tDetail string\n43|}\n44|\n45|func (err *Error) Error() string {\n46|\treturn \"terminal instance refused: \" + err.Code + \" at \" + err.Detail\n47|}\n48|\n49|// refuse builds the refusal for one arm.\n50|func refuse(code, detail string) *Error {\n51|\treturn &Error{Code: code, Detail: detail}\n52|}\n53|\n54|// wrapLanded converts a landed terminalbackend refusal into this\n55|// package's uniform error type, preserving the wire code and the static\n56|// landed detail clause. A non-refusal error is never wrapped: callers\n57|// classify uncoded failures explicitly at their own arm.\n58|func wrapLanded(err error) *Error {\n59|\tvar refusal *terminalbackend.Error\n60|\tif errors.As(err, &refusal) {\n61|\t\treturn &Error{Code: refusal.Code, Detail: refusal.Detail}\n62|\t}\n63|\treturn nil\n64|}\n65|\n66|// ErrorCode reports the wire code of an error produced by this package\n67|// or the landed core, or \"\" when the error carries no wire code. Engine\n68|// callers use it to read backend-reported codes; tests assert the\n69|// literal codes directly on *Error.\n70|func ErrorCode(err error) string {\n71|\tvar refusal *Error\n72|\tif errors.As(err, &refusal) {\n73|\t\treturn refusal.Code\n74|\t}\n75|\tvar landed *terminalbackend.Error\n76|\tif errors.As(err, &landed) {\n77|\t\treturn landed.Code\n78|\t}\n79|\treturn \"\"\n80|}","final_result":true}}}
