{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000caed","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":977,"recorded_at":1780531400001949,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"call_id":"call_01a0b297f2757625b9240f89c32269bc","text":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/doc.go`.\n1|// Package terminstance executes the Terminal Instance lifecycle contract of\n2|// SPEC §4.C over the landed internal/terminalbackend semantic core.\n3|//\n4|// Normative scope is relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec §4.C (lifecycle\n5|// state machine, transition/authorization/idempotency table), §4.B (the\n6|// backend_generation canonical bound), §4.D (capability conditionals\n7|// evaluated at the operation call site), §5.2 (status/unknown discipline),\n8|// §7.A (descriptor generation binding, cited landed) and §13.1 (durable\n9|// terminal entry before provider launch). Worked against\n10|// internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md: §§4.B, 4.C, 4.D, 5.2 and 7.A are\n11|// byte-identical to v0.6.0, while §13.1 carries the v0.7.0 launch-plan\n12|// insertion that precedes step 2 (a pure addition; the durable\n13|// terminal-entry rule text is unchanged).\n14|//\n15|// Composition, not re-implementation: the eight-state enum, the ten-operation\n16|// enum, the ten-effect enum, the transition matrix, the allowed-error sets,\n17|// the idempotency key shapes and the capability registry stay owned by\n18|// internal/terminalbackend (ParseInstanceState, ParseOperation,\n19|// ParseSideEffect, CheckTransition, CheckErrorAllowed, IdempotencyKey,\n20|// CheckOperation, GenerationDigest, CheckProviderDescriptor). Closed-shape\n21|// JSON admission stays owned by internal/environ (DecodeStrictObject,\n22|// CheckStringBounds, CheckUint53Bounds, CheckDigest, CheckUUIDv7,\n23|// CheckTimestamp, CheckSemver). Scalar grammars stay owned by\n24|// internal/scalar. Fencing truth stays owned by internal/fencing\n25|// (Authorize): this package never compares lease tuples itself to decide\n26|// staleness; ObserveFencing reads only the landed park vocabulary. What\n27|// this package owns is the execution layer the landed core deliberately\n28|// leaves out: the AXAuthorization closed object, the RetryDisposition and\n29|// ProviderProofKind closed enums, the mutating-request/response identity\n30|// contract, the per-side-effect recheck loop, the error-to-observation\n31|// mapping, and the durable idempotency receipt store.\n32|//\n33|// Stated bounds (no unsupported claims): no ax command, no tmux/ConPTY\n34|// process control and no provider process exist here; Backend is a modeled\n35|// caller interface. The Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object has\n36|// no parser on trunk (canonicaljson explicitly rejects\n37|// urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding) and the CLI Result 4 bodies\n38|// carry no raw generation member, so the generation bound is enforced on\n39|// the surfaces this leaf owns (operation bodies and results) and cited\n40|// landed for the Provider Protocol 3 descriptor; full Binding-object\n41|// parsing belongs with the provisioning surface. Attach, restore,\n42|// terminate-stale, manifest and probe operations are refused by the engine\n43|// scope gate; restore/terminate-stale recovery belongs to the story's\n44|// final leaf. Events (terminal.created/session.resumed emission) belong to\n45|// the final leaf. On reattach the recorded Binding terminal instance ID is\n46|// authoritative; a request-built descriptor names the request's own fresh\n47|// instance, never the recorded child.\n48|package terminstance","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000caef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":978,"recorded_at":1780531400001951,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"call_id":"call_01a0b297f452728ba0a89ca7af41871d","text":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/errors.go`.\n1|package terminstance\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\n6|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n7|)\n8|\n9|// Wire error codes this package may report. Every code shared with the\n10|// landed core is a const alias of the landed constant, so the literal is\n11|// spelled once on trunk: retyping it here would fork the vocabulary. The\n12|// four row codes the landed core spells only as string literals inside\n13|// its allowed-error table are spelled literally here and pinned equal to\n14|// the landed table by TestRowCodesAreAdmittedByCheckErrorAllowed, which\n15|// drives each literal through the landed CheckErrorAllowed for its row.\n16|const (\n17|\tCodeProtocolError       = terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError\n18|\tCodeUnauthorized        = terminalbackend.CodeUnauthorized\n19|\tCodeUnavailable         = terminalbackend.CodeUnavailable\n20|\tCodePreconditionFailed  = terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed\n21|\tCodeIdempotencyMismatch = terminalbackend.CodeIdempotencyMismatch\n22|\tCodeStaleGeneration     = terminalbackend.CodeStaleGeneration\n23|\tCodeCapabilityUnproven  = terminalbackend.CodeCapabilityUnproven\n24|\tCodeIntegrityFailure    = terminalbackend.CodeIntegrityFailure\n25|\t// CodeTimeout is the §4.C terminal_backend_timeout row code.\n26|\tCodeTimeout = \"terminal_backend_timeout\"\n27|\t// CodeProcessFailed is the §4.C terminal_backend_process_failed row code.\n28|\tCodeProcessFailed = \"terminal_backend_process_failed\"\n29|\t// CodeQuiesceTimeout is the §4.C quiesce_timeout row code, admitted\n30|\t// only on wait-safe-boundary.\n31|\tCodeQuiesceTimeout = \"quiesce_timeout\"\n32|\t// CodeStopTimeout is the §4.C stop_timeout row code, admitted only\n33|\t// on request-stop.\n34|\tCodeStopTimeout = \"stop_timeout\"\n35|)\n36|\n37|// Error is a lifecycle refusal. Code is always one of the Code* constants;\n38|// Detail is a static clause: it never echoes identities, generations,\n39|// keys, digests, or other local data.\n40|type Error struct {\n41|\tCode   string\n42|\tDetail string\n43|}\n44|\n45|func (err *Error) Error() string {\n46|\treturn \"terminal instance refused: \" + err.Code + \" at \" + err.Detail\n47|}\n48|\n49|// refuse builds the refusal for one arm.\n50|func refuse(code, detail string) *Error {\n51|\treturn &Error{Code: code, Detail: detail}\n52|}\n53|\n54|// wrapLanded converts a landed terminalbackend refusal into this\n55|// package's uniform error type, preserving the wire code and the static\n56|// landed detail clause. A non-refusal error is never wrapped: callers\n57|// classify uncoded failures explicitly at their own arm.\n58|func wrapLanded(err error) *Error {\n59|\tvar refusal *terminalbackend.Error\n60|\tif errors.As(err, &refusal) {\n61|\t\treturn &Error{Code: refusal.Code, Detail: refusal.Detail}\n62|\t}\n63|\treturn nil\n64|}\n65|\n66|// ErrorCode reports the wire code of an error produced by this package\n67|// or the landed core, or \"\" when the error carries no wire code. Engine\n68|// callers use it to read backend-reported codes; tests assert the\n69|// literal codes directly on *Error.\n70|func ErrorCode(err error) string {\n71|\tvar refusal *Error\n72|\tif errors.As(err, &refusal) {\n73|\t\treturn refusal.Code\n74|\t}\n75|\tvar landed *terminalbackend.Error\n76|\tif errors.As(err, &landed) {\n77|\t\treturn landed.Code\n78|\t}\n79|\treturn \"\"\n80|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
