ntrol; every other non-kind still refuses. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resume-status-error: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the timeout-coded failed reconciliation read past the uncertain-refusal arm (one behavioral arm in two adjacent checks: ExecuteStatus returns the empty report on every error path, so the timeout must pass both); every other failed read, and every non-empty non-source report, still refuses. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resume-contradiction: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Resumes on exactly the parked contradiction as well as the source; target-proven, unknown and other contradictions still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resume-target: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Resumes on exactly the proven target state as well as the source; contradictory and unknown observations still refuse. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resume-scope-instance: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Reconciles through exactly the Session-scoped lookup instead of the exact instance, adopting a lying instance report; exact reconciliation still refuses it. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resume-complete-key: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Records the completion under exactly a second key instead of the bound one; the identical retry then reconciles instead of replaying. [exit 1]\\nok: N-resume-generation-value: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Reconciles with exactly an empty generation instead of the request generation; the proof then mismatches and the resumption never proceeds. [exit 1]\\nok: N-engine-bind-prelink: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Restores the source on a pre-link store failure for every row except exactly quiesce-input; the quiesce row then fences unavailable. [exit 1]\\nok: N-engine-bind-postlink: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Restores the source for exactly standing receipts as well as for nothing-durable; the hook-error commit then restores instead of fencing uncertain. [exit 1]\\nok: C-control: SURVIVED (want SURVIVED) :: Harmless control: a comment-only edit must survive. [exit 0]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2903,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 726,\