{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d9cf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":2882,"recorded_at":1780531400005759,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2b2-bb0c-72f1-a5d9-47edafbbe3cc"},"task_id":"01a0b2b2-bb0c-72f1-a5d9-47edafbbe3cc","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2b2-bb0c-72f1-a5d9-47edafbbe3cc","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-53-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"terminstance\\\" README.md | head; echo ===; sed -n '1,60p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check README section and LOGBOOK head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"2215:## Terminal Instance lifecycle execution (`terminstance` engine)\\n2217:[`internal/terminstance`](internal/terminstance) executes the Terminal\\n2242:go test ./internal/terminstance -count=1\\n2243:go test ./internal/terminstance -cover -count=1\\n2250:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/terminstance/mutant_harness.py\\n2260:[the task evidence map](internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-kkh1an — Terminal Instance lifecycle execution engine (second leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/terminstance` — the §4.C execution layer over the landed `terminalbackend` core: closed `AXAuthorization` (UUIDv4 lease, uint53 epoch bound, UUIDv7 holder, kind, timestamps, digest) through the `environ` closed-shape discipline, closed `RetryDisposition`/`ProviderProofKind` enums, the `MutationContext`/`MutationResult` identity contract with exact per-row idempotency material, and the `Engine` (durable receipt before first effect, per-effect auth+generation rechecks, source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` post-commit, deadline cancels waiting never committed effects). `stale_fenced` enters only through `fencing` park vocabulary; status is receipt/effect-free and unknown is never absent. Second leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n- REFRESH: rev1 was constructed on `e6fe5c5` and its suite stopped at command 4/30 on the trunk resumesmoke time bomb (fixed as `a12d1bd`); this run refreshed the candidate onto `c3aae73` (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay, 29 stale trunk-changed paths restored to the new HEAD, LOGBOOK/README/decide.go rebased purely additive, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical), inherited the rev1 worktree delta verbatim, and re-verified it against SPEC.v0.7.0 plus the landed owners instead of redoing it.\\n- F1: quiesce-input and request-stop carry no conditional beyond conferral — their spec capabilities are their sole conferring registry rows — so the landed `CheckOperation` decides those rows alone and a second arm restating it would be dead code; the engine's conditional covers only create-headless, wait-safe-plus-provider-iff, and status-provider, where the spec demands more than conferral.\\n- F2: the receipt's no-replace commit needs a separate completion file, because the result is unknown at bind time and updating the receipt in place would break no-replace; pending-without-done is therefore the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` with `status_first` instead of replaying or inventing absence.\\n- F3: the epoch high edge cannot be weakened past `environ`'s own uint53 ceiling (same value, equivalent mutant), so that harness row tightens instead and proves the edge is exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it; the min edge, the delegate's ceiling, and the tightening row triangulate the bound.\\n- F4: closed P3-6 from the predecessor review (the `Decision.Descriptor` doc now states the recorded Binding instance is authoritative on reattach); P3-2/P3-3 stated as unreachable-shape bounds (no `Decide` caller, no checkpoint loader in this package); P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 left to the final leaf with the recovery/events reasons.\\n- F5 (this run): the staging sweep deleted every `*.tmp` unconditionally, so a concurrent `Bind` could lose its live stage and fail its link spuriously — now age-gated (1 min, crash garbage ages out, readers ignore staging names), pinned by keep/sweep tests plus a narrowing row. Also closed this run: the `doc.go` drift claim (§13.1 carries the v0.7.0 launch-plan pure-addition insertion, so \\\"byte-identical in scope\\\" was false — reworded precisely), the missing create entry-deadline and first-effect reported-`stop_timeout` pins (the two stop directions now measured together), the unmeasured kind-mapping/fencing-operation/timeout-code/status-source gates (new rows), the six `checkParams` arms (new rows; the bootstrap row caught a weak `err==nil` assertion, now literal), the Go-level version arms, the malformed-reported-member status arms, and the wire-order sorts (new rows).\\n- F6 (bounds stated, not built): AX-side seam verdicts (uncoded effect → `terminal_backend_process_failed`, uncertain retry → `terminal_backend_unavailable`) sit outside the §4.C row sets, which govern backend reports via `CheckErrorAllowed`; the wait/stop lesser-of-timeout is enforced by the backend wait (validated and carried in `Params`, engine enforces `deadline_at`); document member weakenings masked by a same-detail Go twin carry their narrowing row on the twin.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 68 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 70/70 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\\n- AC: 72 of 72 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`; 70 named top-level tests all present via `go test -list`, 7 cited subtests all `--- PASS`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-SIGKILL pattern. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded chunks with identical flags, 40/40 packages, no DATA RACE; tracecheck `56/569` trunk figures unchanged). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\\n- REWORK (test-only; no production behavior file changed): rev1 was reviewed CHANGES REQUESTED on the story-close half only — its technical body (N1-N3 closure, mutants, fuzz controls, 23/29 AC ratio) was independently reproduced by the reviewer. Rev1 was built on stale base 888ae3d while trunk adopted v0.7.0 (2fc6d50) mid-run. Rev2 refreshed the candidate onto 2fc6d50 (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay: trunk's two v0.7.0 entries kept newest-first, 219okr block carried verbatim below them) and re-based every story-close edit on trunk bytes.\\n- TRACEABILITY: registry work moved into adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (5 new acceptance cases, 3 upgraded bindings: 11.2 partial 3/5, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4); every clause line re-measured against the pinned v0.7.0 document through the production clause inventory (11.2: 7364/7408/7420; 17.1: 15567/15589/15602; 17.4: 15661). The invented 11.3#18 binding is dropped — no production code parses a digest-identity array, so 11.3 stays the carried unevidenced stub and `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` was not ported. Digest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally, new clauses re-measured; every other binding still rederives byte-equal).\\n- P3 GAPS (all closed with a failing-without-it test): opaque-body object gate over `health.get` (`[]`/`null`/`\\\"x\\\"`/`42`/duplicate-member → ErrFrame) + `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` now feeds raw bodies with an I-JSON object oracle (the naive `&& op !=` plant is vacuous — the stale `err` still propagates — so the committed probe restructures the gate); changed-body retry after a committed effect → literal `idempotency_mismatch` with a single retained journal (one-off J1 overlay kills the new test, staging still passes); body-fuzzer oracle bound stated explicitly (member-name + object + round-trip only; bounds/vocabularies owned by the unit suite) + hello-body-extra seed in `FuzzUnknownFields`; exact 8388608-admit/8388609-refuse encode edge; `ErrVersionMismatch` class pinned in the error-schema lanes; literal `[2 3 4]`/`[5]` offer sets in the N2 rows; nonce-alphabet plant widened to the full unpadded standard-base64 class (two-arm `RawStdEncoding` narrowing, no new import).\\n- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 41 killed / neutral passed / error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev4 — ax pane rework: fold-only newest, resumed-checkpoint closure, replay signal\\n- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev3 (1 P1 class at two sites, 1 P2, 8 P3): the strict lease/fold equality is deleted — the fold is the sole newest authority and a successor lease's checkpoint is the handoff base at takeover time that never moves, so the only asserted fact is the implication \\\"a checkpoint-carrying winner means the fold published a newest\\\" at one site directly after fencing (launch and restore alike, parked `restore_policy` on a null fold); `Run` derives the profile closure from the checkpoint actually resumed (required checkpoint, else fold newest, else session head), never `Winner.Checkpoint`; `Supersede` reports the commit-race replay and `Run` flips the post-window loser to `reattach`; the window never closes on the lease record, an unfoldable chain fails the run, and the identity record binds its own `session_id`.\\n- F1: an immutable handoff base can only ever imply, never equal, a moving newest — the equality held only until the successor owner's first checkpoint, and relaxing it alone turned the park into a wrong-profile launch, so both sites landed together with the post-takeover lifecycle positive (restore launches with C1's closure) and the wrong-profile plants in both directions through `Run`.\\n- F2: a store-level replay without a signal is a lie at the call site — `Supersede` replayed the winner's receipt but `Run` reported `launch` with a child it did not create; the `(Binding, bool, error)` signal mirrors `Bind`'s `reattached` and flips the outcome, pinned through `Run` with the `AfterStage` hook.\\n- F3: per-object classification cannot be derived from an aggregate error — `Reconcile` liveness shares the generic mismatch code and carries no per-row identity, so the `realmRowUsable` copy is a stated classification-only bound, fail-closed both directions; likewise the handoff-base-to-published binding is the takeover leaf's stated obligation.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 52 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 53/53 with control), including the null-fold conditional row, the closure-source row (a mutant reading `Winner.Checkpoint` again dies), the replay-keeps-launch row, the lease-closes-window row, and the fold-error-laundered row. AC 43/43 re-derived by counting with every named test verified present; the four rev3-unfaithful rows now pin the post-takeover launch positives.\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev3 — ax pane rework: fold newest, per-pair receipts, credential conditional\\n- REWORKED on `2fc6d50` (SPEC.v0.7.0, same headings) after review-verdict-rev2 (1 P1 class, 2 P2, 8 P3): the bootstrap window, checkpoint admission, and journal source binding now read the chain fold's newest checkpoint (`sessstate.Reduce` → `Projection.HasCheckpoint`/`Newest.ID`) instead of the lease record's checkpoint, which is null for every epoch-1 owner; a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold; superseded pairs keep per-operation receipts (`receipts/<op>.json`, no-replace per pair) with the first binding as the in-window anchor; `Run` fails when a checkpoint-carrying winner has no checkpoint store bound; the §4.C credential conditional applies to every caller with `Smoke.Required`, the realm cross-bind accepts any binding object, and dead (expired/pre-reboot) realm evidence refuses the typed `capability_unavailable`.\\n- F1: lease records are immutable content-addressed blobs — `CreateLease` mints epoch-1 with a null checkpoint and only a takeover mints a checkpoint-carrying successor — so \\\"the winning lease's checkpoint\\\" can never be the newest-checkpoint authority; the ordinary same-host story (stopped with C on epoch 1) is the test that catches the confusion at all three gates (window/admission/journal) at both `Decide` and `Run`.\\n- F2: per-pair receipts keep the §4.1 replay contract (\\\"identical retry replays it\\\", keyed `session_id + \\\"/\\\" + bootstrap_operation_id`) while the first-binding anchor keeps the in-window mutual exclusion the link race proved; `SessionBound` scans anchor-or-receipts so a crash between installs cannot reopen the window.\\n- F3: `Reconcile` fails before the realm arm runs, so dead realm evidence needs a refusal mapping, not a wider gate: the mapping fires only when the caller needs the realm row, submitted a realm row, and none is usable — a usable row plus an unrelated backend fault keeps the backend class.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 47 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 48/48 with control), including one narrowing mutant per P1-1 conditional (window-fold, null-fold ×2, newest, agreement ×2) and the RV7 losing-epoch row the rev2 suite survived. AC 43/43 re-derived by counting (rev2's \\\"41 of 41\\\" restated a 43-row denominator; the reviewer measured 39/43).\\n- REVERSAL (P1-1, stated explicitly): this entry's \\\"a successor lease's handoff base must agree with the fold\\\" is FALSE as of rev4 — a successor lease's `checkpoint_id` is the handoff base at takeover time and never moves, while every checkpoint the successor owner publishes afterwards lands on the chain, so the strict equality held only until the successor owner's first checkpoint and parked every session that was ever taken over. The fold is the sole newest authority; the only asserted fact is the implication \\\"a checkpoint-carrying winner means the fold published a newest\\\" (one site, directly after fencing), and the profile closure comes from the checkpoint actually resumed, never `Winner.Checkpoint`.\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev2 — ax pane rework: authority, window, closure, realm\\n- REWORKED on `888ae3d` after review-verdict-rev1 (18 findings): event authority through `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` with local-hold-only emission and the §5.7 fold gate (`sessstate.Reduce`); realm authorization through the admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to host binding/build/generation (bare boolean removed); bootstrap window closed by the winner's `HasCheckpoint` with atomic `Supersede`; checkpoint admission bound to the winning lease and session; profile from the checkpoint closure (`DeriveForHeads`); journal source bound to the lease checkpoint; non-interactive `headless_creation` conditional; remote non-interactive parks per §4.2 step 5.\\n- F1: a park decision's stale/unverified presented token never authors — `Emit` presents the winning tuple itself, so verified local-winner parks (stale, material, checkpoint) emit while remote/unverified/ambiguous/handoff parks refuse; `Run` pre-checks local hold + foldability and parks without evidence rather than manufacturing a §5.2 collision.\\n- REVERSAL (P3-8, stated explicitly): rev1 F1's \\\"both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`\\\" is FALSE as of rev2 — `attach_remote`, `takeover_offer`, and every remote park author no chain event, because the local wrapper cannot append under another host's lease (§5.2: the winning owner serializes state-changing events); the decision itself is the parked evidence.\\n- F2: the bootstrap window is the winner's `HasCheckpoint`, not a clock: in-window changed ops refuse `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes, post-window new ops supersede via staged rename; the `binding-*.tmp` sweep is age-gated (1 min) so a concurrent live stage is never deleted.\\n- F3: resume profile is the checkpoint closure, not the head: `Run` loads the winner's heads even when the checkpoint is not otherwise required, so a head-only or losing-lease `profile.changed` never drives launch (§2.4, §13.10).\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 35 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with control); reviewer's RM1/RM2/RM4 survivors now killed by `TestRunTornLeasePropagates`, `TestDecideRemoteOwnerPrecedesMaterialization`, `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`. AC 41/41 re-derived with the six previously unfaithful rows re-pinned.\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/axpane` — the pure `Decide` core (`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked|refused`), the `Run` orchestration over real stores, the durable bootstrap `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` binding store, §5.2 event authorship, and the §7.A descriptor builder. Every check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`, `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`, `terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented. First leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n- F1: `fencing` launch entries refuse — not park — foreign sessions, malformed tokens, and lapsed grants, so the wrapper's `refused(lease_conflict)` rows for foreign/expired inputs compose directly; only remote/ambiguous/unverified/absent/stale ownership parks. Remote parks resolve locally to `attach_remote` (interactive + attach admitted) or `takeover_offer`, and both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`.\\n- F2: the tuple gate must precede profile mapping in arm order: `ResolveMapping` re-checks the tuple internally, so mapping-first would wear tuple refusals as `profile_mapping_unavailable`. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call stays as fail-fast ordering; weakening it alone is unobservable (defense in depth, stated in TRACEABILITY.md).\\n- F3: `terminalbackend.Reconcile` maps generation drift to the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation` (not the generic mismatch), and `create` is conferred by both `durable_disconnect` and `headless_creation` — the unproven vector must deny both. `sessckpt.Get` re-attests through `sessrepo` on every read, so checkpoint admission composes through the read path.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 19564,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4891,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
