{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d9d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":2884,"recorded_at":1780531400005763,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"call_id":"call_01a0b2b2b30b739798252dce643fa646","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-53-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"terminstance\\\" README.md | head; echo ===; sed -n '1,60p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check README section and LOGBOOK head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"2215:## Terminal Instance lifecycle execution (`terminstance` engine)\\n2217:[`internal/terminstance`](internal/terminstance) executes the Terminal\\n2242:go test ./internal/terminstance -count=1\\n2243:go test ./internal/terminstance -cover -count=1\\n2250:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/terminstance/mutant_harness.py\\n2260:[the task evidence map](internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-kkh1an — Terminal Instance lifecycle execution engine (second leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/terminstance` — the §4.C execution layer over the landed `terminalbackend` core: closed `AXAuthorization` (UUIDv4 lease, uint53 epoch bound, UUIDv7 holder, kind, timestamps, digest) through the `environ` closed-shape discipline, closed `RetryDisposition`/`ProviderProofKind` enums, the `MutationContext`/`MutationResult` identity contract with exact per-row idempotency material, and the `Engine` (durable receipt before first effect, per-effect auth+generation rechecks, source restore pre-commit, `unavailable`+`status_first` post-commit, deadline cancels waiting never committed effects). `stale_fenced` enters only through `fencing` park vocabulary; status is receipt/effect-free and unknown is never absent. Second leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n- REFRESH: rev1 was constructed on `e6fe5c5` and its suite stopped at command 4/30 on the trunk resumesmoke time bomb (fixed as `a12d1bd`); this run refreshed the candidate onto `c3aae73` (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay, 29 stale trunk-changed paths restored to the new HEAD, LOGBOOK/README/decide.go rebased purely additive, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical), inherited the rev1 worktree delta verbatim, and re-verified it against SPEC.v0.7.0 plus the landed owners instead of redoing it.\\n- F1: quiesce-input and request-stop carry no conditional beyond conferral — their spec capabilities are their sole conferring registry rows — so the landed `CheckOperation` decides those rows alone and a second arm restating it would be dead code; the engine's conditional covers only create-headless, wait-safe-plus-provider-iff, and status-provider, where the spec demands more than conferral.\\n- F2: the receipt's no-replace commit needs a separate completion file, because the result is unknown at bind time and updating the receipt in place would break no-replace; pending-without-done is therefore the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable` with `status_first` instead of replaying or inventing absence.\\n- F3: the epoch high edge cannot be weakened past `environ`'s own uint53 ceiling (same value, equivalent mutant), so that harness row tightens instead and proves the edge is exactly 9007199254740991 by refusing it; the min edge, the delegate's ceiling, and the tightening row triangulate the bound.\\n- F4: closed P3-6 from the predecessor review (the `Decision.Descriptor` doc now states the recorded Binding instance is authoritative on reattach); P3-2/P3-3 stated as unreachable-shape bounds (no `Decide` caller, no checkpoint loader in this package); P3-1/P3-4/P3-5 left to the final leaf with the recovery/events reasons.\\n- F5 (this run): the staging sweep deleted every `*.tmp` unconditionally, so a concurrent `Bind` could lose its live stage and fail its link spuriously — now age-gated (1 min, crash garbage ages out, readers ignore staging names), pinned by keep/sweep tests plus a narrowing row. Also closed this run: the `doc.go` drift claim (§13.1 carries the v0.7.0 launch-plan pure-addition insertion, so \\\"byte-identical in scope\\\" was false — reworded precisely), the missing create entry-deadline and first-effect reported-`stop_timeout` pins (the two stop directions now measured together), the unmeasured kind-mapping/fencing-operation/timeout-code/status-source gates (new rows), the six `checkParams` arms (new rows; the bootstrap row caught a weak `err==nil` assertion, now literal), the Go-level version arms, the malformed-reported-member status arms, and the wire-order sorts (new rows).\\n- F6 (bounds stated, not built): AX-side seam verdicts (uncoded effect → `terminal_backend_process_failed`, uncertain retry → `terminal_backend_unavailable`) sit outside the §4.C row sets, which govern backend reports via `CheckErrorAllowed`; the wait/stop lesser-of-timeout is enforced by the backend wait (validated and carried in `Params`, engine enforces `deadline_at`); document member weakenings masked by a same-detail Go twin carry their narrowing row on the twin.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 68 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 70/70 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\\n- AC: 72 of 72 row