{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dc13","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":3172,"recorded_at":1780531400006339,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2b4-76cd-7503-9fea-77a4d21d85a3"},"task_id":"01a0b2b4-76cd-7503-9fea-77a4d21d85a3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2b4-76cd-7503-9fea-77a4d21d85a3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(282 line(s) above)\n283|  provider process do not exist here.\n284|- Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed-object parsing: no parser\n285|  exists on trunk (`canonicaljson` explicitly rejects\n286|  `urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding`); the generation bound is\n287|  enforced on the surfaces this leaf owns and cited landed for the\n288|  Provider Protocol 3 descriptor (`terminalbackend` checkGeneration\n289|  arms). Full Binding parsing belongs with the provisioning surface.\n290|- CLI Result 4 summary: no landed Result 4 body carries a raw\n291|  generation member (`internal/cliresult` carries none by grep), so\n292|  there is no surface to witness the bound on; consistent with §4.E\n293|  (generation is host-local, non-replicable).\n294|- Attach, restore, terminate-stale, manifest, probe: refused by the\n295|  engine and body scope gates. Restore/terminate-stale recovery and\n296|  terminal binding events belong to the story's final leaf.\n297|- Create is receipt-scoped: receipt, transition, target and headless\n298|  rules execute; the full create body (Binding, Entrypoint,\n299|  presentation transport) belongs to provisioning.\n300|- Credential-realm conditional: credential need is not modeled on the\n301|  engine path.\n302|- Protocol_version membership in the admitted probe list is enforced at\n303|  registry admission (landed), not re-derived per operation; the\n304|  operation gate enforces grammar plus major 1 through the landed\n305|  `CheckVersionTuple` arms.\n306|- The per-code disposition mapping is the leaf's contract where the\n307|  spec pins the vocabulary but not the mapping; every arm is pinned\n308|  literally and mutated.\n309|- AX-side seam emissions are outside the §4.C row sets: the row sets\n310|  govern backend reports (gated through the landed\n311|  `CheckErrorAllowed`), while an uncoded effect outcome classifies\n312|  `terminal_backend_process_failed` and an uncertain retry refuses\n313|  `terminal_backend_unavailable`, both with after `unavailable` and\n314|  `status_first` per the row recovery columns. Engine deadline\n315|  cancels before any attempt report `replay_same` on every row\n316|  (nothing was attempted); a backend-reported `stop_timeout` maps\n317|  through `DispositionFor` (`status_first` even uncommitted) because\n318|  the graceful wait ran. The two stop directions are pinned together\n319|  (`TestExecuteEntryDeadlineCodes`,\n320|  `TestExecuteBackendRowErrorSets`).\n321|- The wait/stop \"lesser of request deadline and timeout\" bound is\n322|  enforced by the backend wait (modeled here), which reports a coded\n323|  `quiesce_timeout`/`stop_timeout` proving non-commit; the engine\n324|  validates the timeout members (`uint53[1..3600000]`, carried in\n325|  `Params`) and enforces the `MutationContext` deadline.\n326|- Document member arms delegate their grammars to the landed\n327|  `environ`/`scalar` owners and are pinned literally through the\n328|  parse entries; where a Go-level twin re-validates with the same\n329|  detail, the Go twin carries the narrowing row (a document-side\n330|  weakening alone is masked by the twin). The body scope gate and\n331|  the body member-set gate have no twin and carry their own rows\n332|  (`N-body-scope`, `N-body-members`). The engine scope gate is\n333|  fail-fast ordering: admitting an operation past it is masked by\n334|  the `checkParams`/`KeySegments` scope defaults firing the same\n335|  detail (defense in depth, stated); `kindFor` is not redundant and\n336|  carries `N-engine-kind-map`.\n337|- The fencing operation must be launch-class (`restore`, equivalent\n338|  to `activation` on the stale arms and chosen for the terminal\n339|  domain); the non-launch entries refuse stale tokens instead of\n340|  parking them, measured by `N-fencing-operation`.\n341|- `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract; the final\n342|  leaf carries the registry bindings and the re-pin.\n343|\n344|## Inherited advisories (predecessor P3, for the record)\n345|\n346|- P3-6 closed by this leaf: the `Decision.Descriptor` doc in\n347|  `internal/axpane/decide.go` now states the recorded Binding\n348|  terminal instance ID is authoritative on reattach; this package's\n349|  `doc.go` states the consumer side.\n350|- P3-2 bound stated: this leaf adds no I/O-free `Decide` caller (the\n351|  engine never calls `Decide`), so the missing-closure input shape is\n352|  unreachable from this package; the pure-core hardening stays with\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
