{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dd09","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b291-18f0-70a0-900f-0c92cf0433eb"},"sequence":3295,"recorded_at":1780531400006585,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cb7c4ff2-7892-4304-8de0-3769502303db"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2b5-07f9-7991-ac4e-97a0d1c9bff2"},"task_id":"01a0b2b5-07f9-7991-ac4e-97a0d1c9bff2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2b5-07f9-7991-ac4e-97a0d1c9bff2","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-18\n-\n-### TASK-260830-kkh1an — Terminal Instance lifecycle execution engine (second leaf)\n+## 2026-09-18\n+\n+### TASK-260830-kkh1an rev3 — Terminal Instance rework: resumption, remote fencing, row gates\n+- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (no P1; P2 F1/F2 production, P2 E1/E2 evidence, 7 P3; the rest — harness 70/70, 72/72 ratio, real-kill seam, hygiene — reproduced by the reviewer): F1 makes the same-key retry after `status` executable — a bound key without its completion reconciles through the production status entry, resumes under the same receipt when status proves the source (quiesce, stop-not-closed, create-absent: one effect set, one completion, one receipt), and refuses uncertain on target/contradiction/unknown; F2 fences the stale incarnation under a remote winner by asking the landed gate from the winner's own host (no local tuple comparison), from active/parked/quiescing, keeping the winning token as no-transition; E1 pins the create row's entry auth/generation/headless gates (no receipt bound) plus the committed second-effect timeout; E2 rotates lease+generation before the third stop effect and drifts the reported session on both status paths plus all five other axes both ways; P3-1 restores the source on pre-link store failure (post-link/lookup failures fence uncertain); P3-2 bounds fencing sources to the live states; P3-3 pins the deadline instant on both entries; P3-4 adds attach/none to the kind negatives; P3-6 replaces the kind twin with a landed `TransitionAuthorization` accessor (registered in the backend's census/inventory/audit batteries); P3-7 and `holder_host_id`-unbound recorded as stated leaf contracts.\n+- REVERSAL (F2 of the rev2 entry, stated explicitly): \"pending-without-done is the honest interrupted state and its retry refuses `terminal_backend_unavailable`\" is FALSE as of rev3 for the proven-source case — the retry now reconciles through status and resumes under the same receipt when status proves the source, refusing uncertain only while the observation is genuinely unknown (target/contradiction/read-failure). TRACEABILITY rows 70/71 reworded to the resumed behavior; the `StoreHooks` doc sentence now states reconcile-instead-of-replay.\n+- F1: an uncertain retry must reconcile through the production status entry rather than accept a caller-supplied report — a cached proof would let a stale source authorize a re-issue, while the engine's own exact-instance read cannot go stale; the query binds all six identity axes so a lying backend cannot authorize a resumption, and re-issue under the same key relies on the backend's own key binding (§13.13 safe_retry: never a second key, never a second process).\n+- F2: the landed gate's arm order (\"the operative fact beats the credential\") hides staleness under a remote winner behind `remote_owner`, so the projection must ask twice — once as the local host, once relative to the winner — and fence only when the relative verdict is stale; both questions stay inside `fencing.Authorize`, which is composition, not a second model.\n+- F3: the resumption's `err != nil` and `report.State != source` checks are one behavioral arm in two adjacent checks (status returns the empty report on every error path), so its narrowing row spans both and admits exactly the timeout-coded failed read; either half patched alone is masked by the other.\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 98 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 100/100 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. The eleven rev2 reviewer narrowings are mirrored as committed rows with committed killers. No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\n+- AC: 84 of 84 rows driven through production entries by named tests (rows 1–72 keep rev2 numbers with 70/71 reworded; rows 73–84 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/terminstance/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-SIGKILL pattern on both the quiesce and create seams, each extended through status-gated same-key resumption. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-kkh1an — Terminal Instance lifecycle execution engine (second leaf)\n","final_result":true}}}
